,-2,1,"nit: remove `const` from this member and `std::move(...)` here to avoid a copy"],["6179f17d_c832ab75",113,-2,1,"could this live in //base/test with other test support stuff?"],["6add4e77_66fd1540",109,-2,1,"`std::string()` rather than `\"\"` to construct an empty string"],["70c51c24_ead19aa8",110,-2,1,"nit: `{}` or `std::string()`"],["77555af1_819d7eeb",109,-2,1,"consider `static constexpr std::string_view kAppName = ...` as per https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/chromium-dev/c/OXxJy5L96jI/m/tRZHIeZwAgAJ."],["802eab22_e5666781",110,-2,1,"consider `CHECK_EQ(channel, version_info::Channel::STABLE)` here"],["aadaf7fc_eba2a0b6",109,-2,1,"nit: use `base::StrCat({...});` rather than `+=` to combine strings."],["c9449cb1_61bccf4a",114,-2,1,"It's not obvious that this file is 'nix-only. Consider renaming it? In addition, maybe include build/build_config.h here, and then add: `static_assert(BUILDFLAG(IS_POSIX) && !BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC));`…"],["ce03d9c1_026c68be",115,-2,0,"maybe it's 17 years too late for this, but should the environment variable have a different name for non-Google Chrome builds?"],["f58964b6_573dbcc3",116,-2,1,"Are the code in the if/else section the same, except for chrome vs. chromium? Maybe just conditionally define the expectation strings instead?"],["f7b5a8fc_f1f3a9c0",110,-2,1,"replace this with `case version_info::UNKNOWN` so that we get a compile error here if anyone ever adds a new enumerator -- we'll most likely need to adjust the logic here in that case."],["fde72fdd_2fe6fa20",115,-2,1,"this file does more than just channel-related stuff. is `channel.h` really the best name? if everything here is specific to `CHROME_VERSION_EXTRA` (which i confess to not liking in //base -- it's a…"],["1cba5b13_cb1fe139",117,-1,1,"apologies for not mentioning this in the first round: pass by non-const ref rather than by pointer since this is a non-optional input as per…"],["b58af7cd_995c59c5",83,-1,1,"very optional nit: if `env` is not used after this 